summary:
  A cover lookup that is in the air when the online covers are switched
  off goes on to its next request, and paints what it finds.

history:
  lookupAlbumArt asks the switch once, at its door. The chain behind it
  asked only whether the track was still the same, so a request that was
  out when the listener switched the covers off came home empty and sent
  the next one: two requests where one was due, measured with the real
  engine and answers held back by hand. A cover that came home that way
  was painted as well. The answer is now dropped at the callback, before
  it is looked at. This mutant lets it through again.

target:
  package/contents/ui/ArtworkEngine.qml

find:
                  if (!cfg.albumArtEnabled) return;
                  kind = url ? SearchLogic.artKind(kind) : "";

replace:
                  if (false) return;
                  kind = url ? SearchLogic.artKind(kind) : "";

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_artworkengine.qml::test_covers_switched_off_end_a_chain_that_is_in_the_air.
  Line-neutral.
